  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nThe last few days I have seen Homarr using a lot more memory than normal and appears to grow the longer without restarting the container. I've seen it as high as 2.5GB. It's currently sitting at 1.4GB after about a day.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nNot sure, but these are the integrations and widgets in use: media streams, download clients, calendar, weather, media requests, several iframes (dashdot), docker status.\n\nI also have my dashboard as my browsers homepage, and so every time I open a new window or tab it loads the dashboard. I can increase memory usage by spam opening the dashboard and closing the tabs. Memory doesn't seem to go back down once all tabs are closed.\n\n### Impact\n\nWorkaround is to just restart the container and that will be good for a day or two.\n\n### Additional information\n\nUbuntu Server \n\nPastebin: https://pastebin.com/5SQh9E3d\n\nI can run any commands to get more detailed logs. Just let me know which ones.\n\n### Version\n\n1.70.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\nBrave",
